1
00:00:05,633 --> 00:00:10,300
You're paid in USDC on three chains, and your landlord wants proof.

2
00:00:10,333 --> 00:00:12,333
Annal keeps one book for all of it.

3
00:00:12,367 --> 00:00:15,233
Every line is copied from the payment's own log.

4
00:00:16,067 --> 00:00:23,700
A reactive contract on Lasna watches Circle's USDC on Ethereum, Base and Unichain for payments to you.

5
00:00:23,733 --> 00:00:27,567
When one lands, it calls back the book on Base Sepolia.

6
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:29,267
Nothing else can write there.

7
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:33,033
Opening a book is one transaction.

8
00:00:33,067 --> 00:00:35,033
It's the only thing you ever do.

9
00:00:46,167 --> 00:00:49,367
Seconds later, Reactive confirms it's watching.

10
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:51,233
Nobody pressed a button.

11
00:00:55,167 --> 00:00:57,467
A client pays you on Unichain.

12
00:01:05,100 --> 00:01:08,900
There it is: copied from Unichain's log, written on Base.

13
00:01:10,900 --> 00:01:13,667
Pay on Base, and it prints in the same book.

14
00:01:24,200 --> 00:01:31,400
Every line opens to its trail: the payment, the reactive transaction on Lasna, and the callback that wrote it.

15
00:01:31,433 --> 00:01:35,300
And the reader's own browser checks it against the origin chain's receipt.

16
00:01:36,767 --> 00:01:40,833
Someone sent this wallet 500 of a token called USD Coin.

17
00:01:40,867 --> 00:01:42,600
Explorers list it.

18
00:01:43,300 --> 00:01:45,000
The book printed nothing.

19
00:01:45,033 --> 00:01:47,800
Reactive only listens to Circle's contracts.

20
00:01:53,367 --> 00:01:55,267
Even the owner can't write a line.

21
00:01:55,300 --> 00:01:57,000
The chain refuses it.

22
00:01:57,033 --> 00:01:59,267
There's no owner and no admin.

23
00:01:59,300 --> 00:02:01,167
Nobody types in this book.

24
00:02:02,567 --> 00:02:04,367
Your landlord opens a link.

25
00:02:04,400 --> 00:02:08,633
No wallet, and no trust in you: just lines they can check.

26
00:02:11,733 --> 00:02:18,833
Twenty-four real payments across three chains: every one printed, a median of one second after its block.

27
00:02:20,100 --> 00:02:22,500
One income book for every chain you're paid on.

28
00:02:22,533 --> 00:02:27,200
Every line is copied from the payment's own log, and links back to it.
